When I [last wrote](/blog/modmox-on-the-map), a run was a walk across a generated map
of placeholder Stages, fighting the same purple demon piloting one of three test
decks, for no reward. Every piece of the loop existed and none of it had any
character.

Five days and 28 commits later there's a place called Kitty Keep, and the eight cats
above live there. The work fell into five chunks:

## A Stage that's somewhere

Kitty Keep is white's first Stage, and the first one that isn't a slate rectangle.
Each Stage can now have a Map Backdrop, one tall pixel art picture as wide as the
screen and as tall as the whole map. It scrolls with the map as you climb, so the
nodes sit on its ground. Kitty Keep's is a meadow with a castle and open sky.

Scattered over that is Scenery. A Stage lists the kinds it has and how many of each,
and the map places them at random from the Run Seed, so the trees, flower bushes and
hay bales land somewhere new each run. They're kept on a mask painted over the meadow,
which leaves out the castle and the sky, and they keep clear of every node, every
link and each other. A spot that breaks a rule is thrown away and rolled again, the
same way the map itself is. Some of the Scenery is animated, which in Kitty Keep means
ginger, gray and black cats sitting around in the grass.

## Villains with faces

The demon is retired from Kitty Keep. A Villain's portrait is now drawn by hand at 32
by 32 pixels, after the art of a real Magic card's first printing, turned to face the
front. The Stage has three Lesser Villains, starting with Charmed Stray, the gray cat
at the top left. Steppe Lynx and Kemba are among its Elites, and the Boss can be Zar
Ojanen, Arahbo or Brimaz, picked when you enter. Each has a deck of its own.

<img
	src="/modmox/portrait-faces.webp"
	alt="Two rows of three pixel art portraits at five times their size. The top row is a gray cat looking ahead, wincing with its eyes shut and head tilted, and with its eyes closed calmly. The bottom row is a crowned lion king looking ahead, grimacing with bared teeth, and with his eyes closed"
	width="560"
	height="380"
	loading="lazy"
	class="post-pixel"
/>

Every portrait comes in three pictures. Next to the normal one there's a Pain
Portrait, the same character the moment after being hurt, wincing and knocked a
little aside, and a Blink Portrait with the eyes closed and nothing else changed. The
plan is for the pain one to show longer the more life was lost, and for the blink to
flicker by every few seconds so the character seems alive. The game doesn't show
either yet. They're drawn now so that every Villain arrives with all three.

<img
	src="/modmox/gulls-perch-villains.webp"
	alt="Four pixel art bird portraits at four times their size: a white hydra of goose heads, a pale crowned eagle with raised wings, a dark blue bird with a skull-like beak, and a white-headed bird in gold armor holding a staff"
	width="612"
	height="168"
	loading="lazy"
	class="post-pixel"
